{"id":415,"date":"2016-05-16T12:57:20","date_gmt":"2016-05-16T12:57:20","guid":{"rendered":"http:\/\/masterbadminton.dev\/yonex-french-open-2011-mens-singles-semi-finals-lee-chong-wei-v-chen-long\/"},"modified":"2016-08-31T16:47:00","modified_gmt":"2016-08-31T16:47:00","slug":"yonex-french-open-2011-men-singles-semi-final-leechongwei-chenlong-html","status":"publish","type":"post","link":"https:\/\/masterbadminton.com\/yonex-french-open-2011-men-singles-semi-final-leechongwei-chenlong.html","title":{"rendered":"Yonex French Open 2011 Men&#8217;s Singles Semi Finals: Lee Chong Wei v Chen Long"},"content":{"rendered":"<div id=\"ContentColumn\">\n<div class=\"Liner\">\n<div style=\"float: left;\"><\/div>\n<p>&nbsp;<\/p>\n<table border=\"1\" width=\"80%\">\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Tournament<\/strong><\/td>\n<td>Yonex French Open 2011 Semi Finals (Super Series)<\/td>\n<\/tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Location<\/strong><\/td>\n<td>Paris, France<\/td>\n<\/tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Date of Match<\/strong><\/td>\n<td>29 October 2011<\/td>\n<\/tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Category<\/strong><\/td>\n<td>Men Singles<\/td>\n<\/tr>\n<\/tbody>\n<\/table>\n<p>&nbsp;<\/p>\n<p><iframe loading=\"lazy\" src=\"http:\/\/www.youtube.com\/embed\/0B8x4ypWH3o\" width=\"560\" height=\"315\" frameborder=\"0\" allowfullscreen=\"allowfullscreen\"><\/iframe><\/p>\n<p>This match was the major highlight of the Yonex French Open 2011.<\/p>\n<p>Lee Chong Wei faced Chen Long, who beat him in the last <i>two<\/i> OSIM BWF tournaments (<a href=\"leechongwei-chenlong-yonex-japan-open-2011-men-singles-finals-analysis.html\">Yonex Japan Open 2011<\/a> &amp;amp <a href=\"yonex-denmark-open-2011-finals-leechongwei-chenlong.html\">Yonex Denmark Open 2011<\/a>).<\/p>\n<p>This meant that Lee Chong Wei had lost 2 consecutive finals in the OSIM BWF tournaments.<\/p>\n<h3>Could Chen Long Cause Another Upset?<\/h3>\n<p>Badminton fans were really uncertain on whether Chen Long would defeat Lee Chong Wei for the <i>third<\/i> time. Malaysian fans were definitely concerned.<\/p>\n<p>Prior to this match, Lee Chong Wei had reached the finals of <i>every<\/i> tournament he played in 2011.<\/p>\n<p>This meant that if he had lost this match to Chen Long, it would be the <i>first<\/i> time Lee Chong Wei would get knocked out in the semi finals.<\/p>\n<h3>Hard Fought Battle<\/h3>\n<p>Fortunately for the Malaysian, Chong Wei had proved his number 1 ranking by beating Chen Long. This also ended Chen Long&#8217;s winning spree against him.<\/p>\n<p>This was fought in 3 thrilling badminton games at the score of 23-21, 17-21, and 21-15.<\/p>\n<p>Lee Chong Wei managed to keep calm in this match.<\/p>\n<p>He had more variations in his shots. He also played a few impressive deceptive shots, which managed to put Chen Long out of position most of the time.<\/p>\n<p>The only problem with the world no.1 was that he wasn&#8217;t really confident at the front of the court. Chong Wei made a couple of unforced errors at the net area throughout the match.<\/p>\n<p>Overall, this match is worth watching again.<\/p>\n<div class=\"retnvbx1\"><\/div>\n<div class=\"fb-comments-intro-ns\">\n<div class=\"retnvbx\"><\/div>\n<h3><span class=\"teelmeww\">Tell me what you think!<\/span><\/h3>\n<p>What do you think about what you just read? Leave me a comment below.<\/p>\n<\/div>\n<div id=\"COMMENTING\" class=\"fb-comment\">\n<div class=\"fb-comments\" data-href=\"http:\/\/www.how-to-play-badminton.com\/yonex-french-open-2011-men-singles-semi-final-leechongwei-chenlong.html\" data-num-posts=\"15\" data-width=\"100%\"><\/div>\n<h3 class=\"fblikeste\">Like Masterbadminton.com?<\/h3>\n<p>&nbsp;<\/p>\n<div id=\"fb-root\"><\/div>\n<p><script><![CDATA[\n(function(d,s,id){var js,fjs=d.getElementsByTagName(s)[0];if(d.getElementById(id)){return;}js=d.createElement(s);js.id=id;js.src=\"..\/connect.facebook.net\/en_US\/all.js#xfbml=1\";fjs.parentNode.insertBefore(js,fjs);}(document,'script','facebook-jssdk'));\n><\/script>\n\n\n<div align